<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>9.11.1: Maximum and Minimum Value of a Function</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02518</md:content-id>
    <md:title>9.11.1: Maximum and Minimum Value of a Function</md:title>
    <md:uuid>4a961abe-608d-4ec6-92cb-3afc89a17960</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Examine the graph that represents the function, \(f\), defined by \(f(x)=(x−4)^2+1\).</para>
<para><figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/4246a818d67db1e72a333d627b6aa12064c74adc"/></media></figure></para>
<para>Use this graph to answer questions 1 - 2.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><title>Warm Up Activity</title><exercise data-content-id="72cfface-ac05-4874-bfc9-69aefdf085cd"><problem><para>
      <para>\(f(1)\) can be expressed in words as "the value of \(f\) when \(x\) is 1." Find or compute:</para>
      <para>Enter the value of \(f\) when \(x\) is 1</para>
      <para>Enter the value of \(f\). </para>
    </para></problem><solution><para>10</para><para>
      <para>Nice try! The correct answer is 10.</para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section><para>Examine the graph that represents the function, \(g\), defined by \(g(x)=-(x−12)^2+7\).</para>
<para><figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/ce9c6929c1bd313d327c435153311f2fd64e328f"/></media></figure></para>
<para>Use this graph to answer questions 3 and 4.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="ae384efe-9cca-4fce-a616-2fb8bf7b91ad"><problem><para>
      <para>\(g(9)\) can be expressed in words as "the value of \(g\) when \(x\) is 9." Find or compute:</para>
      <para>Enter the value of \(g\) when \(x\) is 9</para>
      <para>Enter the value of \(g\). </para>
    </para></problem><solution><para>-2</para><para>
      <para>Nice try! The correct answer is -2.</para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
</document>
